             :intent
             "seon.cluster contract-findings' referrer query ([:find [?sym ...] :in $ % [?changed ...] [?attribute ...] :where (affected ?key ?changed) [?arity ?attribute ?key] [?function :seon.fn/arities ?arity] [?function :seon.fn/sym ?sym]], the recursive affected rule, ?attribute over :seon.fn.arity/input-refs, output-refs and guard-refs) read 942 index nodes, allocated 303 MB and took 120 ms on a fresh connection over a clone of default's store (warm: 7.8 ms, 7.5 MB), for 0 rows with three changed schema keys (fork eb404fa1 and 6f3b61f6 alike, dh-fix bench.clj :affected). Work should be proportional to the schemas reached and their referrers. Done when the same probe reads nodes proportional to its answer (diagnose the plan: variable attribute pattern, rule fixpoint scans) with a regression on node reads.",
