 #:seon.task{:ns seon.db,
             :name "an-agent-transact-reports-the-runs-open-datoms",
             :kind :function,
             :intent
             "An SCI form (seon.db/transact! [{:seon.ns/name 'scratch.rrecw}]) in an MCP run answers a tx report of 26 datoms of which 1 is the agent's: the run row (seon.turn/id, agent, situation, opened-tx, reply, reply-size, starting-ns), two evaluation intent rows and the seon.db/receipt stamp ride the agent's write because custody prepends the run's open (seon.db/*open*, absent-call) to the first durable write of a form (default 722f110df, agent r-record, tx 536872944). The agent sees Seon's machinery datoms as its own write's result. Correct: an agent's transact! commits and reports only its own data; the turn's record is written by the turn's one settlement.",
             :must-read [seon.db/absent-call seon.db/transact!],
             :created-by #:db{:id 51289}}
 #:seon.task{:ns seon.db,
             :name "an-identity-join-scans-the-whole-ref-attribute",
             :kind :namespace,
             :intent
             "A query [?x :identity-attr ?input] [?y :ref-attr ?x] [?y :a ?v] ... is planned by Datahike as an entity group scanning the whole AEVT range of the ref attribute before the unique lookup binds ?x: work proportional to the store's history, not the answer. One (+ 1 2) visits 54,000 index nodes (run-receipts 19,000; runtime-analysis-batch 11,340; next-ordinal, continuing-reply?, spent-runs, branch-errors, evaluation-terminal-data, entity-emission, form-problem). Passing the identity as a lookup-ref input: run-receipts 19,004 -> 22 visits, 14.7 MB -> 0.9 MB. Root decides: Datahike planner fix (recommended) or caller rewrites. Done when one (+ 1 2) visits a number of nodes independent of the store's evaluation count.",
             :must-read
             [seon.db/q
              seon.eval.drive/run-receipts
              seon.fn/runtime-analysis-batch],
             :evidence
             ["docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/growth/growth-notes.md"],
             :created-by #:db{:id 116513}}
 #:seon.task{:ns seon.db,
