             :kind :function,
             :intent
             "seon.db/q with an or clause whose variable is then joined to another pattern costs about 65-88 ms and 135-160 MB per input binding, while datahike.api/q on the same query and database takes 8-10 ms for 142 bindings. Reproduce in JVM mode on default (722f110df, 2026-10-07): (seon.db/q '[:find ?d :in $ ?sym :where (or [?e :seon.fn/sym ?sym] [?e :seon.test/sym ?sym]) [?e :seon.program/definition-digest ?d]] db 'seon.db/q) 88 ms / 160 MB for one row; with [?sym ...] over 10 symbols 658 ms / 1.36 GB, 40 symbols 2.3 s / 5.4 GB; without the definition-digest join 1 ms. It is the whole cost of seon.turn/code-currency (142 symbols: 9.6 s / 19 GB; root's 672 symbols: about 42 s), hence the 43.6 s read-only system turn that ran past the 32 s MCP bound (profile: code-currency 15 calls, 114.6 s total, max 41.9 s). Done when seon.db/q on these shapes stays within a small constant factor of datahike.api/q, proven by a table test over or/or-join followed by a join, scalar and collection bindings.",
             :must-read [seon.db/q seon.turn/code-currency],
             :evidence
             ["docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/plan-research/r-context-notes.md"],
